  "worked_solution": "We take the derivative of each term and then add them, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-csc\u2061x-2{x}^{3}+cos\u2061x) \\\\  & =(-csc\u2061xcot\u2061x)-2\\cdot 3{x}^{2}+(-sin\u2061x) \\\\  & =-csc\u2061xcot\u2061x-6{x}^{2}-sin\u2061x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ in the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{\u2032}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =-csc\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{4})cot\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-6{(\\frac{\\pi }{4})}^{2}-sin\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 1-6\\cdot \\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{16}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{2}-\\frac{3}{8}{\\pi }^{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{3}{8}{\\pi }^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
